From 4681e66b29f6e9b543a1b1f3485a8f13e78b53c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 20:01:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 385/403] Unified: formulas follow an object deleted and made
 again under the same name

FreeCAD kept the formula's text but not its link: the formulas that used
a crank's joint, made again as "Revolute", were computed once and then
stood still, silently (engine field test 0.8.1). Before a recompute of a
file where objects were made, a formula naming an object that is there
but not linked is set again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
